\n\n
aadisc is a bash mini project developed by Aadi. This is a terminal utility which can be used to create and check for aliases. The featurelist is still expanding. This is purposefully made less versatile than it can be. Currently supported flags and features are:\n
\n
syntax format aadisc [flag] [args]\n
\n
FLAGS:\n
\n
\t -c = This flag checks wether the alias already exists or not. It takes the name of the alias as an arguement\n
\t -s = This flag shows what alias points to it takes the alias name as the only arguement\n
\t -r = This flag is used to replace and already existing shortcut\n
\t -R = This flag is used to remove and already existing shortcut\n
\t -n = This flag creates new alias the arguements are alias name and path \n
\t -l = This flag lists all the shortcuts
\n
\t\t aadisc -n [alias name] [alias path]\n 
